# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Main portal — browser-facing configuration
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Leave this RELATIVE ("/api/v1") when deploying to Vercel.
#
# Next.js rewrites (next.config.js) proxy /api/v1/* server-side to
# the EC2 backend. Keeping the URL relative makes every browser
# request same-origin, so httpOnly session cookies work and CORS is
# never evaluated. An absolute URL here (e.g. http://IP:4000/api/v1)
# makes the browser call the backend directly, which breaks cookies
# because the backend is plain HTTP and sets secure/SameSite=none.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined at BUILD time, not runtime — after
# changing this you must redeploy, a restart is not enough.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=/api/v1

# Map tiles. Defaults to OpenStreetMap standard raster tiles when unset.
# Set to CartoDB Positron for a cleaner grey road basemap:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_TILE_URL=https://{s}.basemaps.cartocdn.com/rastertiles/voyager/{z}/{x}/{y}{r}.png

# No Mapbox token is needed. The app uses Leaflet + OpenStreetMap;
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAPBOX_TOKEN was a leftover from an earlier Mapbox
# attempt and is referenced nowhere in src/.